    "created_at": "2018-05-28T08:42:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-28T08:42:54Z",
    "body": "I was initially, but I'm wondering if what browsers do here is preferable, since even though you can read such responses as the result of navigation (`<iframe>`) or image loads, that doesn't allow you to read the bytes of all such responses (e.g., a PDF).\r\n\r\nSo I think we probably want to keep this restriction intact where we can (and break it for navigation, images, scripts?, ?).",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
