    "created_at": "2018-05-29T14:21:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-05-29T14:21:53Z",
    "body": "I think we should avoid reseting back to basic tainting where we can.  This is consistent with how cors requests can never become same-origin again once they cross an origin boundary.  It would be a bit unexpected to me to make no-cors less restrictive.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
